+# Flow image recovery: uploaded references shown as tiles (v7.0.90)
+
+## What the job showed (shot_020, 2026-10-25)
+- The request was journaled as `submission_uncertain`, with no acknowledgement.
+- After the persisted project reopened, the probes downloaded for the two new tiles were the
+  two uploaded references: `location_master.jpg` and `character-aradhya-aaa37613-0.png`
+  (the journal records both as references, checked by checksum and visual match).
+- No generated image appeared in the project in any attempt. This is consistent with the
+  recorded data, but it does not prove whether Flow generated one.
+- The generation wait counted the two references as fresh output. After 30 s it returned
+  `Multiple distinct images require exact request correlation`, so the exact classifier never
+  decided anything. Three recovery attempts ran the same way, and the job was left paused.
+
+## Cause
+Uploaded references are listed in the project grid under URLs that differ from the pre-submit
+baseline. The baseline therefore does not exclude them, and the wait sees them as new output.
+The journal already classifies them, but the wait did not use that.
+
+## What changed
+- `engine/flow_image_transaction.py`: the references the journal has already classified (by
+  checksum or visual match, in this project) are added to the wait's baseline. Only those are
+  excluded; tile order is never used.
+- `engine/providers/flow_browser.py`: `wait_for_agent_generation(..., transactional_images=True)`
+  returns after the stability window instead of failing, so the exact classifier decides. Other
+  callers keep the old failure.
+- `engine/isolated_frame_regeneration.py`: the same exclusion and hand-off for regenerated frames.
+
+## What it does not do
+- It never submits a prompt, clicks Generate, or spends credits. Recovery stays download-only.
+- It does not pick between two real, non-reference outputs. That still stops with
+  `No unique non-reference image yet`, and no file is written.
+- It does not create an image when Flow produced none. If the project shows no generated image,
+  recovery can wait and then stop. A new submission would spend credits, so that is a user decision.
+
+## Verification
+- `tests/test_v790_reference_tile_recovery.py`: references excluded only when classified in this
+  project; recovery classifies the references, waits with them excluded, then commits the one
+  real output; two real outputs stay blocked with no file written; a wait that sees only
+  references does not commit; the waiter hands over only when transactional.
+- Mutation check: removing the exclusion and the hand-off makes 3 of these tests fail.
+- The v743 image-transaction, v787 download and v788/v789 tests still pass.
+
+## What to do with the paused job (shot_020)
+1. Open the saved Flow project and look for a new generated image (not the two references).
+   Do not click Generate.
+2. Install 7.0.90 and resume. Recovery is download-only and will report either the one
+   unique image, or the reason it could not decide.
+3. If Flow shows no generated image for shot_020, send the project screenshot before any
+   resubmission.
+
+## Update
+From 7.0.89: `python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.90/tools/update_v789_to_v790.py . --apply`
+From 7.0.88: first `python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.89/tools/update_v788_to_v789.py . --apply`.
+Stop the dashboard first. Runtime data, jobs, profiles and outputs are never touched.
